    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and real-world logic for me—something I find both challenging and rewarding. My father’s education was limited, but my mother’s curiosity in physics sparked an early interest. Though I never pursued formal study, I’ve always enjoyed problem-solving, especially when it connects to music or cycling (my hobbies). It’s a tool, not just a subject.",
